<decision #track.adopt-halfcode-resource-tree-for-eidolon-apps.root-separation apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" { priority = "P0" status = "accepted" durable_candidate = true } (
  <question ?01M0QP3JTE1J56VZ0K9S4B7HSY>
  How are ResourcePackage roots related to the workflow authoring workspace?
  </?01M0QP3JTE1J56VZ0K9S4B7HSY>
  <answer (
    <raw-answer ?01M0QP3JTE1J56VZ0K9S4B7HSZ>
    They are separate authorities.
    </?01M0QP3JTE1J56VZ0K9S4B7HSZ>
    <decision-text ?01M0QP3JTE1J56VZ0K9S4B7HT0>
    Eidolon binds optional global/workspace ResourcePackage roots under `.eidolon/resources`; `.eidolon/workflows` remains the mutable workflow authoring/session root and is not implicitly scanned or converted.
    </?01M0QP3JTE1J56VZ0K9S4B7HT0>
    <rationale ?01M0QP3JTE1J56VZ0K9S4B7HT1>
    Treating the current directory of independent workflow manifests as a package would invent a host Catalog and merge authoring with the normalized read model.
    </?01M0QP3JTE1J56VZ0K9S4B7HT1>
    <evidence ?01M0QP3JTE1J56VZ0K9S4B7HT2>
    Resource registry architecture and integration tests.
    </?01M0QP3JTE1J56VZ0K9S4B7HT2>
  )>
  <confidence ?01M0QP3JTE1J56VZ0K9S4B7HT3>
  0.98
  </?01M0QP3JTE1J56VZ0K9S4B7HT3>
  <reversibility ?01M0QP3JTE1J56VZ0K9S4B7HT4>
  moderate
  </?01M0QP3JTE1J56VZ0K9S4B7HT4>
)>

<decision #track.adopt-halfcode-resource-tree-for-eidolon-apps.single-generic-authority apiVersion="codument.tech/v1alpha1" { priority = "P0" status = "accepted" durable_candidate = true } (
  <question ?01M0QP3JTE1J56VZ0K9S4B7HT5>
  Which layer owns resource discovery, layering and content identity?
  </?01M0QP3JTE1J56VZ0K9S4B7HT5>
  <answer (
    <raw-answer ?01M0QP3JTE1J56VZ0K9S4B7HT6>
    Halfcode exclusively.
    </?01M0QP3JTE1J56VZ0K9S4B7HT6>
    <decision-text ?01M0QP3JTE1J56VZ0K9S4B7HT7>
    The Eidolon adapter SHALL call Halfcode public load/compose/content-identity APIs and SHALL NOT walk package roots, parse Catalogs, implement shadow rules or compute a competing registry revision.
    </?01M0QP3JTE1J56VZ0K9S4B7HT7>
    <rationale ?01M0QP3JTE1J56VZ0K9S4B7HT8>
    A host-specific generic registry would recreate the Sparrow-era resource manager and violate the mission boundary.
    </?01M0QP3JTE1J56VZ0K9S4B7HT8>
    <evidence ?01M0QP3JTE1J56VZ0K9S4B7HT9>
    Halfcode adapter and static authority scans.
    </?01M0QP3JTE1J56VZ0K9S4B7HT9>
  )>
  <confidence ?01M0QP3JTE1J56VZ0K9S4B7HTA>
  0.99
  </?01M0QP3JTE1J56VZ0K9S4B7HTA>
  <reversibility ?01M0QP3JTE1J56VZ0K9S4B7HTB>
  low
  </?01M0QP3JTE1J56VZ0K9S4B7HTB>
)>
